  "verbalization": "Neogitogenin appears to have a shared target relationship with M-phase phosphoprotein 8 through multiple indirect pathways. The evidence suggests that Neogitogenin acts as a target of several compounds, including Pseudoaeruginosin KT554 and Thaliglucinone, which in turn target M-phase phosphoprotein 8. Similarly, Neogitogenin also targets Solute carrier family 22 member 7, which is a target of Isoderrone, both of which also target M-phase phosphoprotein 8. This indicates a potential pathway where Neogitogenin influences M-phase phosphoprotein 8 through different molecular intermediates. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism where Neogitogenin may modulate M-phase phosphoprotein 8 via distinct but related targets, suggesting a broader role in cellular processes involving the M-phase. The evidence supports a link between Neogitogenin and M-phase phosphoprotein 8 through a series of molecular interactions, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated.",
